 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to requests for absentee ballots",
    "basePrintNo": "S8783",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8783-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8-400, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8783\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to requests for absentee\nballots\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections one and two of the bill amend Section 8-400 of the election law\nby removing provisions prohibiting receipt of absentee ballot applica-\ntions prior to thirty days before the date of the election for which the\nabsentee ballot is requested.\n\nSection two of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow boards of elections to receive absentee ballot\napplications more than thirty days before the applicable Election Day.\nThis will ease the administrative burden on boards of elections by\npermitting more absentee ballots applications to be approved and corre-\nsponding absentee ballots to be sent to voters on an earlier date than\ncurrent deadlines allow. This will also benefit voters and prevent\ndisenfranchisement of voters who do not receive their ballots in a time-\nly fashion due to either delays in administration or the postal service.\nThis is especially important during a time when there are increased\nrequests to vote by absentee due to the novel coronavirus COVID-19.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON LOCALITIES:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\namendments to paragraph (d) of subdivision 2 of section 8-400 of the\nelection law made by section one of this act shall be subject to expira-\ntion and reversion of such paragraph pursuant to section 7 of chapter 91\nof the laws of 2020, when upon such date the provisions of section two\nof this act shall take effect.\n",
